1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
And so I, a Salem vs Ellusia, shall take count slain Sosbom Troyard for my husband, and I also proclaim that a new kingdom is now established for us in Earthspace.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:27,000
My daring and resourceful knights, despite our best efforts, indications are that this war may become more protracted than was foreseen. What should our course of action be, now that we are at this turning point?

3
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Is this the time for orbital knights to squabble amongst themselves over petty power and credit?

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:41,000
No, we must now join together, all under one flag, and fight for the future of verse.

5
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:53,000
As evidence of my earnestness in this regard, I now delegate all of my authority to the lord of this newly reactivated castle, my soon-to-be spouse, Count Troyard.

6
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
This includes the right to decide upon whom to bestow the power to awaken old Noah.

7
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Until the day we achieve victory in this war, I have the utmost faith and hope you will listen to Count Troyard, know that his words are mine, and rally to his side.

8
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:23,000
And we shall do it all for verse.

9
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Tanya then?

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,880
Tanya-

11
00:01:33,880 --> 00:02:03,860
Thank you.

12
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:33,860
Thank you.

13
00:02:33,880 --> 00:03:03,860
Thank you.

14
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:04,700
Yes, sir.

15
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:08,480
But, my lord, for those knights who are anxious regarding this situation,

16
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:12,660
Her Highness' words must have fallen on their ears like a divine revelation.

17
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:13,800
Revelation?

18
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,680
You are her power now.

19
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:18,760
Her decrees and proclamations were only because of you.

20
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:20,720
And everyone knows this.

21
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:23,580
Tonight's unhappy about the current state.

22
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,240
They were words from on high.

23
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:29,180
Surely they must feel their prayers for a true leader have finally been answered.

24
00:03:29,180 --> 00:03:32,540
You exaggerate.

25
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:37,460
Because the fact is, rebel factions will certainly begin to show up as well.

26
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,280
And that's an area where I think you'll be useful.

27
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,020
Do you wish a display of power?

28
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,740
Is that it, my lord count?

29
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:44,480
No.

30
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:47,700
Engaging with these people will become an endless exercise.

31
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:50,280
So, first we boot them out.

32
00:03:50,780 --> 00:03:53,220
Then we let the proper authorities take it from there.

33
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:54,040
My lord?

34
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:56,940
Princess Asalem's name will be all that's needed.

35
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:01,620
Then, it should be simple enough to strip them of their knighthoods with a random accusation.

36
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:05,060
Do I sense disapproval of this action?

37
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:06,520
No, my lord.

38
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:08,220
In fact, quite the opposite.

39
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:11,800
A true leader stops at nothing to achieve his goals.

40
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:18,480
Ever since the announcement, my lord, if I may be so bold, you seem to be preparing for the very worst.

41
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:26,420
I always wanted to be close to her highness.

42
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,600
My only wish was to be worthy of her.

43
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:34,680
Somehow, someday, to be of service to her.

44
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:36,480
But I...

45
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:43,040
If power is all I can win, then that must become my goal.

46
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:47,320
Is that you, Harklight?

47
00:04:47,820 --> 00:04:48,160
Enter.

48
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:51,460
A lord slain.

49
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:55,180
Yes, Adel Ritzo?

50
00:04:57,240 --> 00:05:02,080
We are satisfied with your ship's deployment and your existing personnel.

51
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:07,700
For the time being, we want your continued support as a current ad hoc commando squad.

52
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:09,440
No objection to those orders, sir.

53
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:13,180
However, as to Princess Asalem's recent speech...

54
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:16,080
That nonsense about founding a new dynasty in Earth space?

55
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:19,560
That is nothing but big talk meant to stir up the Mars Knights.

56
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:21,080
A morale booster.

57
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:23,080
Yes, that might be the case.

58
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:29,020
But then, we also might want to consider that we're looking at a possible escalation of the enemy's war efforts.

59
00:05:29,020 --> 00:05:31,580
Do you think we're just sitting on our hands, doing nothing?

60
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,660
Is that what you're implying here?

61
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:34,800
No, sir.

62
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,720
I did not mean that at all.

63
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:42,120
As far as any new operations, we are in the process of assigning our primary units.

64
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:46,060
Once our strategic planning is finalized, you will be contacted.

65
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:54,140
Captain, you might not care for your status as a commando unit, but there's a limit to how much faith we can put in a ship running on enemy power.

66
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:56,640
That's just the way it is.

67
00:05:56,640 --> 00:06:04,740
I'm amazed you got through that without some outburst.

68
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:05,680
What?

69
00:06:05,780 --> 00:06:07,180
Do you think that's what I should have done?

70
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:09,980
Remember, I'm only here serving as your escort on this.

71
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,380
And anyway, I'm not nearly as naive as I look.

72
00:06:12,620 --> 00:06:13,480
They don't get it.

73
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,280
They don't understand.

74
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,920
I don't think they have a clue what they've got here.

75
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:20,300
And we're doing the best we can.

76
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:21,180
No.

77
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:24,900
I'm not talking about how they're treating us, or the Ducalian.

78
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,880
They're not taking this seriously.

79
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,180
What do you mean?

80
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,580
They don't know the Martians.

81
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:35,920
Right now, the war is going in our favor a tiny bit, and they're acting like it's all one and done.

82
00:06:36,940 --> 00:06:38,080
That's terrifying.

83
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:48,940
I will drain the therapeutic fluid and take Her Royal Highness back to my castle.

84
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:50,760
Tell no one of this.

85
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:53,180
Not even Princess Lamarina.

86
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:55,000
Why not tell me?

87
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:55,860
Do as I say!

88
00:06:58,080 --> 00:06:59,100
I apologize.

89
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:01,480
I did not mean to startle you.

90
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,620
No visitors allowed?

91
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:09,780
Her condition is that serious?

92
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:11,860
Is it a turn for the worse?

93
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:12,900
Perhaps it is.

94
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:16,280
It's a miracle that she has held on as long as she has.

95
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,040
Could we lose her today?

96
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:20,120
Tomorrow?

97
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,420
They say they just don't know.

98
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:25,840
It is possible she could remain in this condition indefinitely.

99
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:27,520
Hmm.

100
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,260
I see.

101
00:07:28,900 --> 00:07:30,560
I can only guess how you feel.

102
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,900
You may well have mixed emotions.

103
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,920
However, she is your only sibling by blood.

104
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:38,100
You are the one feeling sadness.

105
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:39,380
Isn't that right?

106
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:40,660
You, Slane.

107
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:43,140
I must go now.

108
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:46,100
Slane!

109
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:48,100
I forgive you for that.

110
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,140
I forgive you for that.

111
00:07:52,140 --> 00:07:54,720
Even if you broke down and wept in front of me.

112
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:57,620
Shedding tears for her loss.

113
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,400
Because I am...

114
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:03,860
I am already yours.

115
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:12,200
Could I have triggered it?

116
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:13,860
I didn't...

117
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:15,860
Really mean...

118
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:19,400
I always did admire you.

119
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:22,020
You had everything that I did not.

120
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,120
So I hated you too.

121
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:29,800
Still, no need to worry, sister.

122
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:33,440
From now on, I will truly be your substitute.

123
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:38,620
And as for Slane, I will give him the support he needs.

124
00:08:38,620 --> 00:08:44,480
Why am I crying?

125
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:56,160
Hmm.

126
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:58,060
Come on now.

127
00:08:58,180 --> 00:08:58,960
What's up with that?

128
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,140
Are you saying the captain just ditched her here?

129
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:04,360
The captain left me in charge because she thinks I can handle the job.

130
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:06,100
At least that's what she said.

131
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:09,860
But Commander Mitsuzaki has obviously got to be just devastated.

132
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:13,580
Of all people, why pick Lieutenant Marito for a traveling companion?

133
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:14,440
Companion?

134
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,920
Nah, he's more like an escort.

135
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,800
What's this about, Lieutenant Marito?

136
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:19,960
Uh, nothing at all, really.

137
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:22,900
It's just that he went along with the captain to that briefing,

138
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:24,820
so I thought it might be something serious.

139
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:25,800
I see.

140
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:28,340
Well, with that proclamation by the princess,

141
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:31,180
the situation is definitely changing minute to minute.

142
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:34,080
I just find it hard to believe she's gonna marry that count.

143
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:35,780
You care about that?

144
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:37,240
No, but think about it.

145
00:09:37,660 --> 00:09:40,240
Isn't it possible that this big change of heart

146
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:42,440
was because someone close to her felt that way?

147
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:45,660
You know, some deal where she got seduced into it and...

148
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:46,580
Sorry.

149
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:49,280
But we're still not 100% sure, are we?

150
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:51,740
That the princess of Salem in the speech we just heard

151
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:53,120
is the same one who is with us?

152
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,620
She didn't talk like that when she was down here.

153
00:09:55,900 --> 00:09:57,860
To tell you the truth, I have no idea.

154
00:09:58,480 --> 00:10:01,460
Inaho insists she's actually an imposter, but how can we tell?

155
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:04,660
Well, there's no way to know just how much he really can see.

156
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,160
Have you eaten anything?

157
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,140
In a little while.

158
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:14,400
Let me find a good place to leave off.

159
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:16,500
You've been this way since we were just kids.

160
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:19,320
When you're into something, the world fades away.

161
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:19,980
Here.

162
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:21,780
That's great.

163
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:22,440
Thanks, Yuki.

164
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,440
You've heard, right?

165
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:26,760
About the speech of Salem made?

166
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:28,460
Yes.

167
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:33,240
I have to admit, that proclamation seemed to prove everything you've been saying.

168
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:36,200
And it all seems a little too convenient.

169
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:39,180
If that really was the real princess of Salem,

170
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:43,580
she would never think of founding a new kingdom and killing to do it.

171
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,060
Slain Troyard.

172
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:51,640
You mean that douchebag who shot my little brother in the head?

173
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,440
Thank you for caring.

174
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,160
You might want to watch your language, Yuki.

175
00:10:56,160 --> 00:11:01,480
Honestly, it just doesn't matter anymore whether she's real or not.

176
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:04,960
I don't think anyone would listen to her now.

177
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:09,800
Even if she was trying to promote genuine peace between Earth and Mars again.

178
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:15,000
About the attack on Earth, my lord.

179
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:18,180
If there are no problems, I will get preparations underway.

180
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,500
Is all well, my lord?

181
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:23,560
I'm listening.

182
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:25,600
We will proceed as planned.

183
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,700
Yes, sir.

184
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:28,440
And, her highness?

185
00:11:29,020 --> 00:11:30,380
She will wake soon.

186
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:31,420
I know it.

187
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:33,500
I, too, eagerly await that day.

188
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:34,780
Truly, my lord.

189
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:38,120
But, should we also fear it?

190
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:38,600
Sir?

191
00:11:39,960 --> 00:11:40,860
Never mind.

192
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:49,840
Has there been any change at all?

193
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:51,560
No, my lord.

194
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:54,720
They believe she could remain like this for some time.

195
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,420
So then we will wait.

196
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,500
I am accustomed to that, right?

197
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:00,860
I think that she will be very surprised.

198
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:04,600
When she wakes up again, she'll see how much everything has changed.

199
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:06,120
And will I?

200
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:10,320
Will I seem different to her as well?

201
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:15,240
She will think, what a fine man it is you've grown into.

202
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:16,260
I am sure.

203
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:20,980
I shall return.

204
00:12:20,980 --> 00:12:33,700
My lord slain!

205
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:36,080
Tell her it's so.

206
00:12:38,620 --> 00:12:39,760
Tell her it's so.

207
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,020
Oh, my lady.

208
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:43,600
Is it you?

209
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:45,340
My lady's awake.

210
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,580
My lady's awake.

211
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:49,040
She came back.

212
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:51,420
Your highness, it is me, slain.

213
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,160
I'm right here.

214
00:12:53,920 --> 00:12:54,800
Do you see?

215
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:55,980
I'm slain.

216
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:57,660
Slain Troyard.

217
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:01,840
I'm slain.

218
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:03,900
Troyard.

219
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,160
Your highness.

220
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:38,460
I've waited so very long to hear you say my name, to hear you speak again.

221
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:50,980
Do you see me?

222
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:53,480
Don't lie.

223
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:54,840
Let me see.

224
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:55,040
I haven't happened to you.

225
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:59,820
I haven't been hurt.

226
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:29,800
To be continued...

227
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:32,860
I deeply regret causing you worry, Count Baracruz.

228
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:34,400
And what are your plans now?

229
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,680
I have none as of yet, and I have also lost my cataphract.

230
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:43,680
If you wish to ally with Count Troyart, I could intercede on your behalf.

231
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:48,880
About Count Marilsian, I heard of the event. It must be a continuing wound for you.

232
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:55,640
No. Both sides fought fairly, and that was just the way things came out. I have no cause to hold a grudge.

233
00:14:55,640 --> 00:15:05,120
Please, my lord, Count. Troyart is dangerous. Not only did he kill Marilsian, there are even suspicions that he was responsible for the death of Count Sarsgård.

234
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:07,760
Who would say that? Be cautious.

235
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,440
I merely thought you...

236
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:16,160
Hold your tongue, my lord. Obviously, you are the victim of unfounded rumors.

237
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:21,660
I take it you were privileged to hear Princess of Salem's proclamation.

238
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:25,600
There is no one who can stop Count Troyart's illustrious rise.

239
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:29,560
Not with his power including all Noah activation privileges.

240
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:33,160
It would be like fighting a sandstorm on Olympus.

241
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:39,180
If you wish to remain among the orbital knights, I suggest you act wisely.

242
00:15:40,980 --> 00:15:44,520
Count Barocruz has pledged full and unconditional cooperation.

243
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:50,080
Count Zebron and Raffia have yet to make it clear what their allegiances will be.

244
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:53,080
But they appear amenable to acknowledging the new kingdom.

245
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,920
Morale has risen throughout the base.

246
00:15:57,680 --> 00:16:01,820
And we have almost finished going through the list of knights who seem likely to oppose you.

247
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:05,820
We are ready to take forceful steps at a moment's notice.

248
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:07,960
My lord Slane?

249
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:11,800
You seem quite troubled.

250
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:13,960
Pardon, my lord.

251
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:17,080
Is it to do with Princess of Salem's recovery?

252
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,940
You want me to give Adel Ritzo some time off?

253
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:28,320
Yes. Perhaps only for a short time.

254
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:30,680
It's obvious she's out of sorts.

255
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:33,340
The change in Asalem's status was a shock.

256
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,720
I can see that it would be.

257
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:39,000
Tell me, how are you bearing up under all this slain?

258
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,040
I do worry for you.

259
00:16:42,040 --> 00:16:43,760
I thank you for your concern.

260
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:48,800
You see, you are the only one that I know I can count on completely.

261
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:53,940
I will take verse and make it mine, for her highness.

262
00:16:53,940 --> 00:17:14,640
Ma'am, both Dales and Orlov platoons are currently on the march towards the enemy landing castle.

263
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:18,000
Attention, Clydesdale and Mustang platoons.

264
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:20,580
Stay on high alert for the enemy cataphract.

265
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:23,960
As soon as you identify it, attack immediately and take it out.

266
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:33,560
How lovely.

267
00:17:34,060 --> 00:17:34,520
Yes.

268
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:37,820
My lord's lane had this garden made just for you, m'lady.

269
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,120
Is that right?

270
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:44,980
It looks just as it did on Earth.

271
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:45,900
It does.

272
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:49,180
Are your memories coming back from when you were there?

273
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:58,440
Birds.

274
00:17:58,440 --> 00:18:02,080
I was watching them, with that boy.

275
00:18:02,380 --> 00:18:03,500
Inaho Kaisuka?

276
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:04,600
You mean him?

277
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:08,400
Kaisuka.

278
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:28,540
Is there something wrong?

279
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:29,480
Uh, no.

280
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:31,840
Look, m'lady, right over there.

281
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:32,740
Isn't that pretty?

282
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,200
This is Dales' platoon leader.

283
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:43,520
We are closing on the enemy landing castle with Orlov platoon.

284
00:18:44,140 --> 00:18:45,120
Clydesdale platoon.

285
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:55,280
Those arrows have powerful explosive charges on them, so careful, everyone!

286
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:58,340
Bastard!

287
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:02,340
Easy, don't waste your ammunition.

288
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:04,860
The enemy is cloaked and moving real fast out there.

289
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,700
We know they're using arrows, which is probably two.

290
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:08,340
Right.

291
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:11,660
Muzzle flashes would make it a simple matter to pinpoint their location.

292
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:13,840
The arrows must be to avoid that.

293
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:14,960
Optical shielding.

294
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:16,580
An invisibility cloak.

295
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:18,180
Yeah, something like that.

296
00:19:19,020 --> 00:19:20,640
Anyway, it's very ingenious.

297
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:23,080
There's nothing showing on my thermograph.

298
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,540
It doesn't cast a shadow.

299
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:25,820
But it does.

300
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:28,020
You can trust me when I say that it's there.

301
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:29,000
Right.

302
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:34,820
For me, m'lord?

303
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,860
Customize it to suit your taste.

304
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:41,000
I've already discussed your rank in Alt-Noah activation with Princess Lemrina.

305
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,240
Thank you, my lord.

306
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:45,240
The arrow is gone from the bow.

307
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:47,600
Now there is no turning back.

308
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,120
Yes, sir.

309
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:51,820
Now notify the counts at once.

310
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:53,360
Zebron, Raffia, and Olga.

311
00:19:54,120 --> 00:19:55,960
Tell them to swear their allegiance.

312
00:19:55,960 --> 00:20:04,380
Smoke grenades now locked and loaded.

313
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:05,680
And I'm ready here.

314
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:09,440
Fire!

315
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:24,700
He's right.

316
00:20:24,700 --> 00:20:26,540
It definitely exists.

317
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,640
And as long as it's there,

318
00:20:29,420 --> 00:20:31,780
it's going to have an effect on air currents.

319
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:39,740
Target located.

320
00:20:40,060 --> 00:20:40,380
Right.

321
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:41,560
Stand by to fire.

322
00:20:42,040 --> 00:20:42,480
Lieutenant!

323
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:43,840
What is it, Kaiska?

324
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:44,840
On our three o'clock.

325
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:45,500
New enemy!

326
00:20:45,500 --> 00:20:58,880
Closing in from dead ahead.

327
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,700
They're coming at us in a team attack?

328
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:01,860
Overhead two!

329
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:02,640
Incoming!

330
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:11,680
A landing castle.

331
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:13,760
All units, brace for impact!

332
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:43,740
Multiple landing castings.

333
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:44,040
Multiple vessels.

334
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:45,960
Multiple cataphracts.

335
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:48,520
Simultaneous coordination.

336
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:51,560
He's made his move.

337
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:53,360
It's him.

338
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:57,980
So, no time for doubts anymore.

339
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,380
There is no returning from where I am now.

340
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:14,100
Billy.

341
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,300
elly's son dugup.

342
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:18,420
Hmm.

343
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:19,600
You're so old.

344
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:20,420
It says they look the beautiful relação among you.

345
00:22:20,420 --> 00:22:21,440
Take it.

346
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:23,540
Bokutats và

347
00:22:23,540 --> 00:22:28,220
Thank you.

348
00:22:53,540 --> 00:23:00,540
Hasta la fin.

349
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:29,540
Let's believe the beginning of the beginning

350
00:23:29,540 --> 00:23:37,540
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh

